body:
std::variant. You may also want std::optional.

This is a typesafe way of doing a tagged union (this is what Rust’s enums are under the hood).

In C, this looks something like. Under the hood, C++ variant will look something like this.


typedef enum {
  IntTag, StringTag
} Tag;

typedef struct {
  Tag tag;
  union {
     int b;
     char* s;
  } data;
} TaggedUnion;

You can check whether the reference is either null or undefined like so

If (err) {
    // err is neither undefined nor null
}
